# Citation metadata for PlastidToolSuite (Citation File Format 1.2.0).
#
# Authorship note (deliberate, 11/10/2026): the author below is the project, not a list of people.
# Who is named on a citable artifact is the team's decision (CLAUDE.md → who decides: what goes in
# a manuscript is the PI's), and it must be settled BEFORE the DOI is minted — a Zenodo deposit
# records its authors permanently. Replace `authors` with the real list at that point; the rest of
# this file needs no change.
#
# `doi:` is absent on purpose: the release's DOI does not exist until Zenodo mints it from the
# GitHub release (docs/release.md). A placeholder here would be the kind of plausible-looking
# untruth this project exists to avoid.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PlastidToolSuite in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "PlastidToolSuite: a toolkit for plastid and mitochondrial genome analysis"
abstract: >-
  A command-line toolkit for plastid (chloroplast) and mitochondrial genome analysis: genome
  statistics and structure, gene content, codon usage, introns, SSR, repeats, substitutions
  (Ts/Tv), nucleotide diversity, barcodes, Ka/Ks, population genetics, synteny, gene-name
  unification, annotation by reference transfer, and NCBI submission files. Every run writes its
  own directory with its tables, a draft report, and the name, version and command line of every
  external tool it used.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "PlastidToolSuite contributors"
license: MIT
license-url: "https://github.com/tridovan/plastid-suite/blob/main/LICENSE"
repository-code: "https://github.com/tridovan/plastid-suite"
url: "https://github.com/tridovan/plastid-suite"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-11"
keywords:
  - plastome
  - chloroplast genome
  - mitochondrial genome
  - bioinformatics
  - comparative genomics
  - microsatellites
  - codon usage
